One page runs to two sheets: page 2 of the 10-page edition. The scorecards are 112 by 110 mm with their text at 9 pt, and they do not fit on one sheet beside the page's words, so the cards sit at the top of the next sheet. Smaller cards would put their text under the 9 pt floor. If that page should be one sheet, the cards could be drawn smaller with fewer values (the designer), or the page could be shorter (the storyteller); otherwise it stands as built.

The historian's two findings on the sample (manuscript/sample/first-ten-pages.md) are word changes to my sample. The editions supersede it, so I have not changed it; it waits on the editor's word whether the sample lives on (my board 008).

